Below is a step-by-step set of exploratory BigQuery SQL statements – from simple inspection to full monthly ranking – that you can run to identify the most-purchased “other” products (and their quantities) among customers who bought the **Google Red Speckled Tee**, for the three months starting November 2020.  
Each query is limited to 20 rows so you can quickly preview the data before running bigger jobs.

```sql
-- Description: Quick look at any rows that actually contain products (non-empty `items`)
SELECT
  event_name,
  ecommerce.total_item_quantity AS total_qty,
  items
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109`
WHERE ARRAY_LENGTH(items) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Inspect distinct product names that appear on 9-Nov-2020
SELECT DISTINCT
  i.item_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE i.item_name IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Purchase lines that contain the Google Red Speckled Tee in November 2020
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS event_date,
  user_pseudo_id,
  i.item_name,
  i.quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE LOWER(i.item_name) LIKE '%google%red%speckled%tee%'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Distinct November-2020 customers who bought the Tee
SELECT DISTINCT
  user_pseudo_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE LOWER(i.item_name) LIKE '%google%red%speckled%tee%'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Top “other” items and their quantities bought by those November customers
SELECT
  i.item_name  AS other_item,
  SUM(i.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE user_pseudo_id IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
             UNNEST(items) AS j
        WHERE LOWER(j.item_name) LIKE '%google%red%speckled%tee%'
          AND event_name = 'purchase')
  AND LOWER(i.item_name) NOT LIKE '%google%red%speckled%tee%'
GROUP BY other_item
ORDER BY total_quantity DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: December-2020 – most-purchased “other” items for Tee buyers
SELECT
  i.item_name AS other_item,
  SUM(i.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE user_pseudo_id IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`,
             UNNEST(items) AS j
        WHERE LOWER(j.item_name) LIKE '%google%red%speckled%tee%'
          AND event_name = 'purchase')
  AND LOWER(i.item_name) NOT LIKE '%google%red%speckled%tee%'
GROUP BY other_item
ORDER BY total_quantity DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: January-2021 – most-purchased “other” items for Tee buyers
